                <pb facs="0345" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <head>Mr. Harvey to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 298.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 23, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to communicate herewith a
                    copy of a note which has just reached me from the United States consulate at
                    Madeira, having reference to the suspicious steamer Laurel, to which the
                    attention of our public agents had been recently called by telegraphic
                    despatches and correspondence of Mr. Dudley at Liverpool.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES E. HARVEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
